   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "01 TEXT TO PBR (SDXL, STANDARD)\n\nWHAT IT DOES\nType a material -> SDXL makes a TILEABLE image (circular padding in the model and VAE) -> de-light -> height, normal, AO, roughness, metallic, ORM. Fast, runs on 8 GB VRAM.\n\nQUICK START\n1. Edit the Positive Prompt (change the MATERIAL).\n2. Queue (Ctrl+Enter). Check the 3x3 Tiling Check, then collect the maps (ComfyUI/output/PBR_Material/).\n3. Seams? New seed. Light left in? Raise De-light strength.\n\nSETUP (one time)\n\n1. ComfyUI (latest): https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI\n\n2. PBR Studio Nodes (INCLUDED): copy folder custom_nodes/PBR_Studio_Nodes into ComfyUI/custom_nodes/\n   (or run install_pbr_studio.py, see START_HERE.md). Test prompts and sample images: examples/TEST_PROMPTS.md. No extra pip packages.\n\n3. Depth Anything V2 node (height maps)\n   cd ComfyUI/custom_nodes\n   git clone https://github.com/kijai/ComfyUI-DepthAnythingV2\n   pip install -r ComfyUI-DepthAnythingV2/requirements.txt   (use ComfyUI's own Python)\n   Model (99 MB) auto-downloads to ComfyUI/models/depthanything/ on first run. Manual:\n   https://huggingface.co/Kijai/DepthAnythingV2-safetensors/resolve/main/depth_anything_v2_vits_fp32.safetensors\n\n4. Seamless Tiling node (GPL-3.0, you install it, it is not redistributed here)\n   cd ComfyUI/custom_nodes\n   git clone https://github.com/spinagon/ComfyUI-seamless-tiling\n\n5. SDXL checkpoint -> ComfyUI/models/checkpoints/\n   https://huggingface.co/stabilityai/stable-diffusion-xl-base-1.0/resolve/main/sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors\n\nThen restart ComfyUI, load this workflow, press R to refresh models. Red nodes? Manager > Install Missing Custom Nodes.\n\nOUTPUT: see QUICK START above.\n\nIMPORT INTO YOUR ENGINE\nBlender: Albedo -> Base Color (sRGB). Normal -> Normal Map node (OpenGL), Non-Color. Roughness/Metallic -> Non-Color. Height -> Displacement node.\nUnreal: Normal format = DIRECTX in node \"Normal Map\". ORM texture: sRGB OFF, compression \"Masks\": R=AO, G=Roughness, B=Metallic.\n3ds Max / V-Ray / Corona: DirectX normal; Roughness and Metallic as non-color maps.\nUnity URP / glTF: OpenGL normal. (Unity HDRP uses its own mask-map layout, not ORM.)\nNormal looks inverted? Switch OpenGL <-> DirectX in the Normal Map node."
   ],
   "title": "READ ME FIRST: 01 TEXT to PBR (SDXL, Standard)",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 101,
   "type": "Note",
