   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Workflow 01: keep the wording, change only [MATERIAL].\nWorkflow 05: type just the material, one per line. The picker adds the wording for you.\n\nFULL PROMPT (01):\nphotograph of [MATERIAL], seamless tileable PBR texture scan, top-down orthographic view, flat overcast diffuse lighting, no shadows, photorealistic real-world material, natural imperfections, high detail, sharp focus, 8k\n\nTESTED MATERIALS (surface setting in brackets):\nweathered red brick wall with grey mortar (rough) | mossy cobblestone pavement (rough) | travertine stone wall (rough) | rough grey concrete with small pits (rough) | dry cracked desert soil (rough) | asphalt with fine gravel (rough) | grey granite floor tiles (rough) | rusty corroded metal plate (rough, Metallic: bright_areas_only) | dark oak wood planks (flat) | light birch plywood (flat) | weathered teak decking boards (flat) | beige linen fabric weave (flat) | rough off-white plaster wall (flat) | white marble with grey veins (polished)\n\nDid not look realistic in tests: leather, terracotta roof tiles, clay ground. Use a photo (workflow 02) for those.\nFull list and sample images: examples/TEST_PROMPTS.md"
   ],
   "title": "Material Presets & Prompt Styles",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 102,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    1380,
    -780
   ],
   "size": [
    560,
    720
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 27,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "KEY SETTINGS\n- De-light: strength 0.9, light_scale 0.12 (lower = removes smaller shadows), shadow_highlight_compress 0.35.\n- Height: depth_weight = big shapes, detail_weight = fine detail from the albedo.\n- Height (v2.1): set 'surface' in the Height Map node: rough (stone, brick, concrete), flat (wood, fabric, plaster) or polished (marble, glazed tile, chrome) for near-flat relief. 'auto' reads the material name in batch mode and otherwise fades out depth that does not follow the texture.\n- Normal: strength 1.5 (raise for deeper relief). Pick OpenGL or DirectX.\n- AO radius 0.01 / strength 1.0.  Roughness: base 0.65, variation 0.25 (invert flips bright/dark).\n- Metallic: constant 0.0 or 1.0.\n\nTROUBLESHOOTING\n- Red nodes: copy PBR_Studio_Nodes, install Depth Anything / Seamless Tiling, restart ComfyUI, press R.\n- Seams visible: new seed, or (photo) lower blend_overlap,.\n- Normal map inverted in your engine: switch OpenGL <-> DirectX.\n- Height noisy: lower detail_weight or raise Normal smooth_px.\n- Out of VRAM: close other GPU apps, or use 768 px resolution.\n\nHONEST NOTES\n- Height, AO and roughness are image-based ESTIMATES, great for ArchViz, games and previews, not scan-accurate.\n- De-lighting is a heuristic: it removes large light variations and compresses shadows. Hard baked shadows may remain.\n- Metallic is 0 by default (non-metal). For metal set the Metallic node: constant 1.0, or bright_areas_only for rusty/painted metal.\n- Check every model's license before commercial use."
   ],
   "title": "Settings, Troubleshooting & Honest Notes",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
